  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef is playing a game, which he starts with a score of S=0S = 0S=0. He also has an integer NNN.\n\nIn one move, Chef does the following:\n\n\nUniformly randomly pick an integer XXX between 000 and 2N−12^N - 12N−1 (inclusive of both ends)\nUpdate his score as S→S∣XS \\rightarrow S \\mid XS→S∣X, where ∣\\mid∣ denotes the bitwise OR operation\nFor example, if Chef's current score is S=6S = 6S=6 and he picks X=10X = 10X=10, his new score is 6∣10=146\\mid 10 = 146∣10=14.\n\nChef stops when his score SSS becomes equal to 2N−12^N-12N−1.  What is the expected number of moves Chef performs?\n\nOutput the answer modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7. That is, the answer can be expressed as a fraction P/QP/QP/Q, where gcd⁡(Q,109+7)=1\\gcd(Q, 10^9 + 7) = 1gcd(Q,109+7)=1. Print P⋅Q−1(mod&nbsp;109+7)P\\cdot Q^{-1} \\pmod{\\ 10^9 + 7}P⋅Q−1(mod&nbsp;109+7), where Q−1Q^{-1}Q−1 denotes the modular multiplicative inverse of QQQ with respect to 109+710^9 + 7109+7.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input contains an integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nEach test case contains a single integer NNN.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the expected number of moves Chef performs, modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\leq T \\leq 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤N≤3⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 3 \\cdot 10^51≤N≤3⋅105",
      "Sum of NNN over all test cases do not exceed 3⋅1053 \\cdot 10^53⋅105",
      "Subtasks",
      "**Subtask 1 (30 points):**",
      "1≤N≤1031 \\leq N \\leq 10^31≤N≤103",
      "Sum of NNN over all test cases doesn't exceed 10310^3103",
      "**Subtask 2 (70 points):**",
      "Original constraints"
    ],
