        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n1\n2\n100",
        "output": "2\n666666674\n328238032",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: In each move, Chef chooses either 000 or 111, each with a probability of 1/21/21/2. The game ends as soon as Chef chooses 111. Thus, the probability that the game takes exactly kkk moves is 2−k2^{-k}2−k.\nThe required expected value is then ∑k=1∞k⋅2−k\\displaystyle\\sum_{k=1}^\\infty k\\cdot 2^{-k}k=1∑∞​k⋅2−k, which equals 222.\nTest case 222: In each move, Chef chooses an integer in [0,3][0, 3][0,3]. The answer is 8/38/38/3."
